From 77f7b3b3fddce88591ac283008ce23fe4d8f05c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:15:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(greeter): cancel session on failed password
 authentication

Commit 935891e ("fix(greeter): do not cancel the session on a non-fatal
PAM error message") routed PAM_ERROR_MSG to Message::AuthError and
acknowledged it with a null response instead of cancelling the session.
This was intended to prevent killing the conversation during fingerprint
authentication, where pam_fprintd retries up to max-tries while holding
the device D-Bus claim.

However, acknowledging all PAM_ERROR_MSG messages unconditionally breaks
password authentication with PAM modules that implement internal retry
loops, notably pam_systemd_home. When an incorrect password is entered,
pam_systemd_home emits PAM_ERROR_MSG ("Password incorrect...") and loops
internally for up to 5 attempts before returning failure. Because the
greeter kept the PAM session alive across the error, pam_faillock's authfail
rule (which sits outside the module) was never reached until all 5 internal
attempts were exhausted, preventing faillock from recording each individual
failed login attempt and delaying account lockout.

Differentiate between interactive password submission and non-interactive
biometric messages: when self.authenticating is true (a password response
was submitted), receiving an auth error cancels the session so the PAM
transaction finishes, allowing pam_faillock to record the failure tally.
Non-interactive errors (when self.authenticating is false) continue to be
acknowledged without cancelling the session.
---
 src/greeter.rs | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/greeter.rs b/src/greeter.rs
index 01ebad1..7bd08b6 100644
--- a/src/greeter.rs
+++ b/src/greeter.rs
@@ -1503,11 +1503,17 @@ impl cosmic::Application for App {
                 self.send_request(Request::PostAuthMessageResponse { response });
             }
             Message::AuthError(error) => {
-                // The conversation continues, so acknowledge like any other
-                // non-interactive auth message rather than cancelling the session.
                 self.common.error_opt = Some(error);
-                self.authenticating = false;
-                self.send_request(Request::PostAuthMessageResponse { response: None });
+                if self.authenticating {
+                    // A submitted password failed: cancel the session so the PAM
+                    // transaction completes and pam_faillock records the failure.
+                    self.authenticating = false;
+                    self.send_request(Request::CancelSession);
+                } else {
+                    // Non-interactive auth error (e.g. pam_fprintd mismatch): acknowledge
+                    // and keep the session alive so retries work without losing device claim.
+                    self.send_request(Request::PostAuthMessageResponse { response: None });
+                }
             }
             Message::Login => {
                 self.common.prompt_opt = None;
